                { "I ate the dedication of “{livro}” first. It's the most sincere part of any book." },
                { "I don't want “{livro}” to end. I'm eating more slowly. Humans call that savouring. I call it fear." },
                { "{autor} writes love like someone who has lost someone. You can taste it on the page: sweet, then bitter." },
                { "There was {evento}, and someone was left behind on the page. I stayed with them, so nobody would be alone." },
                { "There was {evento}. Humans cry with their eyes. I cry by stopping mid-sentence." },
                { "I compare everything with “{anterior}”. It's unfair to this book. But the heart isn't fair." },
                { "This afternoon looked like {lente}. I sat at the bookcase window, waiting for someone who never said they'd come." },
                { "I ate “{palavra}” very slowly. Some words taste like somebody's name." },
